  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>|</mo> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow> <mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </math> represent two parallel lines <math> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow> </math>.<br />Also, the equation <math> <mrow> <mrow><mo>|</mo> <mi>x</mi> <mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </math> represent two parallel lines <math> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </math> and <math> <mrow> <mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </math><br /><br />Hence, the four lines combined together represent a parallelogram.<br /><br /><br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0022515_Ans1_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 290px; height: 150px;\" /></strong></u><br /><br /><br /><math><mrow><mtext>Hence, required area</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mn>2</mn> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>+</mo> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>·</mo> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> <mo>=</mo> <mn>8</mn> </mrow> </math>",
